      {
        "n": "Southern Proletariat Music Company",
        "s": "2026-09-20T00:00:00+01:00",
        "e": "2026-09-20T01:00:00+01:00",
        "d": "Dancing might be about our implied dependency on Earth. There are examples of rhythmic workings powerful enough to advance our freedoms. We must harness the pulse which comes from the hip and use the beat as fuel for today and tomorrow. One of our favorite practitioners of Black American music (Esperanza Spalding) asks a simple yet pertinent question: why don’t we dance to [jazz/liberation] music anymore? Southern Proletariat Music Company offers a 60 minute mix documenting the humble historic synastry between music and dance as expressed from Black American southern traditions.",
        "j": null,
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/dancing-2026/episodes/dancing-2026-southern-proletariat-music-company-20th-september-2026"
      },
      {
        "n": "The Spiral Dance w/ Emily E",
        "s": "2026-09-20T01:00:00+01:00",
        "e": "2026-09-20T02:00:00+01:00",
        "d": "Covens often perform a “spiral dance” to cast a circle before rituals. The collective, embodied magic of dance  consecrates a space for performing earthly magic. Besides the music that accompanied these dances, the spiral dance offers a paradigm for creation based on cyclic reciprocity rather than endless growth.",
        "j": null,
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/dancing-2026/episodes/dancing-2026-the-spiral-dance-w-emily-e-20th-september-2026"
